Jenkins Agent need 1GB tmp dir space


Because your EC2 instance runs Amazon Linux 2023, the system handles /tmp differently. By default, it allocates a virtual RAM disk (tmpfs) capped at 50% of your total RAM 

Since you just grew your real hard drive to 30 GB, the absolute best and safest way to increase /tmp storage is to tell Amazon Linux to stop using your limited RAM and use your new disk space instead. This will give /tmp access to your 28 GB of free disk storage. 

Run the following two commands in your terminal to safely switch it permanently: 

optimizing-amazon-linux-2023-for-tiny-ec2-instances/)


Step 1: Mask the systemd memory limitTell the operating system to disable the memory-bound RAM version of /tmp: 



> sudo systemctl mask tmp.mount


Step 2: Reboot the serverTo cleanly cut over all background processes (like your Jenkins agent) to the new disk-based storage, reboot the EC2 instance:

> sudo reboot



